## Using Sass
> Owl uses Dart Sass to build CSS for all main modules and themes. If you don’t know Sass, have a look at their [website](https://sass-lang.com/).

Building from source requires [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) 20.19 or later and npm.

Run `npm run build` to compile the SCSS files, prefix the generated CSS, and create minified variants.

### SCSS Files included

Source files can be found in the [GitHub project]({{ pkg.homepage }}).

```no-highlight
src/
└── scss/
    ├── _animate.scss
    ├── _autoheight.scss
    ├── _core.scss
    ├── _lazyload.scss
    ├── _theme.scss
    ├── _theme.default.scss
    ├── _theme.green.scss
    ├── _video.scss
    ├── owl.carousel.scss
    ├── owl.theme.default.scss
    └── owl.theme.green.scss
```

### Partial modules

Files beginning with `_` are Sass modules used by the three public entry points. `_core.scss` contains the carousel layout, while `_animate.scss`, `_autoheight.scss`, `_lazyload.scss`, and `_video.scss` contain plugin styles.

### _theme.scss

Shared structure for the default and green navigation themes. Configure `_theme.default.scss` or `_theme.green.scss` with Sass `@use` when creating a custom theme.

### owl.carousel.scss

Public entry point that combines the core and plugin style modules.

### owl.theme.*.scss

Generated theme entry points for navigation buttons and dots. For custom Sass configuration and examples, see [BUILDING.md](https://github.com/vDyl/OwlCarousel3/blob/main/BUILDING.md).


